{
  "_comment": "BINARYPIVOT STATIC-ANALYSIS TABLES. Two jobs: (1) stop the string sweep from reporting filenames and Java package names as network infrastructure, and (2) name the packer / installer / app-protector wrapping a sample, which tells the analyst WHY a string sweep came back thin. Extend these as new protectors appear — they change far faster than the code that matches them.",
  "fake_tlds": {
    "_comment": "Trailing tokens that look like a TLD but never are one — file extensions, Android resource classes, server-side script extensions. A bare host token ending in one of these is a filename or identifier ('config.json', 'libapp.so', 'index.php'), not a domain. Matched EXACTLY against the last dot-separated label, and ONLY for tokens found outside a real URL (a host that appeared inside an http(s):// URL is trusted regardless).",
